      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Artistic peaks are just doorways rather than permanent hallways, and ending the story now locks you out of any future potential you never get to explore. The pain of decline is often temporary, while the pain of a book that is never written can last forever. There is always a way to restart, even if it feels impossible right now.",
      "source": "target",
